(:id "port/python/vt/widening" :state :doing :evidence ("internal/codegen/pythontable/widening_test.go: TestPythonVtWidening/ladder (13 declarations — the ten integer widths, a ranged int64, bits(12) and float64 — × 15 wire kinds, with top-bit, small, NaN and infinity payloads, through the straight-line load and the descriptor walk under both pins: verdict, value, widened count and saved bytes are internal/tablewire's, and a refused read leaves the caller's report and buffer untouched), TestPythonVtWidening/ladder-widens, TestPythonVtWideningSites (the one _accepts/_read pair at an arm, an array element and a map key: a widening reads and counts one, a narrowing refuses kind_mismatch with no value, and the float rung decides on the kind pair, not the codec string), TestPythonVtWidening/manifest (k1_as_k2 held to its reports.txt verdict; seven rows skipped by name as not carried yet and NOT proven)" "internal/codegen/pythontable/widening_test.go: TestPythonVtWideningNegativeControl (widen.py broken in a copy, one rule at a time: signed-ladder, rungs-closed, widened-count, narrowing, float-rung; each red on the cell it decides)" "make python-vt-widening-negative-control (make/negative-controls.json row python-vt-widening)") :tested-revision "6d5e30aca482ac696ead749117c3924bdadbed4b" :note "2026-11-15: doing, not done. The rule is proven on small constructs: a field accepts every narrower kind on its own signedness ladder, decoded at the writer's width with the wire kind's sign, held to the declared range and counted widened; a float64 field accepts a finite float32 exactly and a non-finite source refuses non_finite_float; the kind pair alone decides and every other pair, narrowings included, refuses kind_mismatch. Of the corpus widening rows only k1_as_k2 is held by a read. NOT proven: field_scalar_widen, scalars_full_as_2, scalars_edges_as_2, a1_arm_moved_width_as_a2 and previous_form_wide_blob (their units use packet types in tables, which Generate refuses) and list_scalar_widen and map_key_widen (the read refuses unsupported_kind: lists and maps are not carried yet); each is skipped by name on its exact not-carried refusal, and the task stays open until the cards that carry those kinds hold them. Run on Linux x86-64 under the pinned CPython 3.15.2 and 3.11.18 (make dist-python), SCHEMA_SLOW=1, -tags schema_leg_python, at this revision.")
